{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "def is_Diff(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\n    Assumes the input is an integer as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    s_num = str(abs(number))\n    alternating_sum = 0\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(s_num):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        # Position from the right: len(s_num) - 1 - i\n        # Rightmost digit (position 0) is added, next subtracted, etc.\n        if (len(s_num) - 1 - i) % 2 == 0:\n            alternating_sum += digit\n        else:\n            alternating_sum -= digit\n            \n    return alternating_sum % 11 == 0"}
