{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the digits of the given number strictly alternate (d1 d2 d1 d2...).\n    Single-digit numbers are considered undulating.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_number = str(abs(number))\n\n    if len(str_number) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    if len(str_number) == 2:\n        return str_number[0] != str_number[1]\n\n    # For numbers with 3 or more digits, check for alternation.\n    for i in range(len(str_number) - 2):\n        # Check for consecutive identical digits (e.g., 112).\n        if str_number[i] == str_number[i+1]:\n            return False\n        # Check for non-alternating pattern (e.g., 123 where 1 != 3).\n        if str_number[i] != str_number[i+2]:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
