{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(decimal_num):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a non-negative decimal integer to its binary string equivalent.\n    Handles 0 explicitly and builds the binary string from remainders.\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal_num == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    binary_str_parts = []\n    # Assume decimal_num is a non-negative integer based on critical requirements\n    temp_num = decimal_num\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        remainder = temp_num % 2\n        binary_str_parts.append(str(remainder))\n        temp_num //= 2\n\n    return \"\".join(reversed(binary_str_parts))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(number: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a non-negative decimal integer to its binary string representation.\n    Ensures the binary string has no leading zeros, except for the number 0 itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    binary_digits = []\n    temp_num = number\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        binary_digits.append(str(temp_num % 2))\n        temp_num //= 2\n    \n    return \"\".join(binary_digits[::-1])"}
