{"task_id": "Mbpp/101", "solution": "def kth_element(array: list, k: int) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth element in the given array using 1-based indexing.\n\n    Args:\n        array: The list of elements.\n        k: The 1-based index of the element to find.\n\n    Returns:\n        The element at the specified 1-based index.\n\n    Raises:\n        IndexError: If k is out of bounds or the array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        raise IndexError(\"Array is empty, cannot find kth element.\")\n    if not (1 <= k <= len(array)):\n        raise IndexError(f\"k ({k}) is out of bounds for array of length {len(array)}\")\n    return array[k - 1]"}
