{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    This implementation uses dynamic programming.\"\"\"\n\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    # For m >= n (including n=0, m > 0), the Eulerian number is 0.\n    if m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize DP table for n+1 rows and m+1 columns (max m is n-1, so up to n-1)\n    # The table needs to store values for A(i, j) where i goes from 0 to n, and j from 0 to i-1.\n    # We create a table of size (n+1) x (n+1) for simplicity, indexing up to dp[i][i-1].\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: A(0, 0) = 1\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table using the recurrence relation\n    # A(i, j) = (j + 1) * A(i - 1, j) + (i - j) * A(i - 1, j - 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):  # m can range from 0 to i-1\n            if j == 0:\n                # Special case for j=0: A(i, 0) = A(i-1, 0)\n                # The general formula would involve A(i-1, -1) which is 0.\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j] * (j + 1) + dp[i-1][j-1] * (i - j)\n\n    return dp[n][m]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) for permutations of n elements with m ascents.\n    It uses the standard sum formula involving binomial coefficients.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Handle special cases based on business rules for n and m\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    if m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    eulerian_sum = 0\n    # The sum runs from k=0 to m\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        # Calculate binomial coefficient C(n+1, k)\n        N_comb = n + 1\n        K_comb = k\n\n        binomial_coeff_val = 1\n        if K_comb == 0:\n            binomial_coeff_val = 1\n        else:\n            # Apply C(N, K) = C(N, N-K) optimization\n            if K_comb > N_comb // 2:\n                K_comb = N_comb - K_comb\n            \n            # Iteratively calculate binomial coefficient to avoid large intermediate factorials\n            for i in range(K_comb):\n                binomial_coeff_val = binomial_coeff_val * (N_comb - i) // (i + 1)\n        \n        # Calculate the power term (m+1-k)^n\n        power_term = (m + 1 - k)**n\n\n        # Determine the sign for (-1)^k\n        sign = 1 if k % 2 == 0 else -1\n\n        # Add the current term to the total sum\n        eulerian_sum += sign * binomial_coeff_val * power_term\n    \n    return eulerian_sum"}
