{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(data_list, start_index, end_index):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified range (inclusive of both start and end indices).\n\n    Args:\n        data_list: The input list of numbers.\n        start_index: The starting index of the range (inclusive).\n        end_index: The ending index of the range (inclusive).\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of the numbers in the specified range.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If data_list is not a list, or if start_index/end_index are not integers,\n                   or if an element within the range cannot be converted to a number.\n        ValueError: If start_index or end_index are out of bounds, or if start_index > end_index.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'data_list' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(start_index, int) or not isinstance(end_index, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'start_index' and 'end_index' must be integers.\")\n\n    list_length = len(data_list)\n\n    if not (0 <= start_index < list_length or (list_length == 0 and start_index == 0)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Start index {start_index} is out of bounds for list of length {list_length}.\")\n    if not (0 <= end_index < list_length or (list_length == 0 and end_index == -1)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"End index {end_index} is out of bounds for list of length {list_length}.\")\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Start index ({start_index}) cannot be greater than end index ({end_index}).\")\n\n    current_sum = 0\n\n    if list_length == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    for i in range(start_index, end_index + 1):\n        try:\n            current_sum += float(data_list[i])\n        except (TypeError, ValueError) as e:\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} ('{data_list[i]}') is not a valid number.\") from e\n\n    return current_sum"}
