{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all \"even bits\" (0-indexed positions 1, 3, 5, ...) in the\n    given integer. The bits are set up to the most significant bit\n    position of the input number.\n\n    Args:\n        num: The integer whose even bits are to be set.\n\n    Returns:\n        The integer with its even bits set.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine the most significant bit position (0-indexed)\n    # For num=10 (binary 1010), bit_length() is 4, so max_bit_pos is 3.\n    max_bit_pos = num.bit_length() - 1\n\n    even_bits_mask = 0\n    # Iterate through even bit positions (1, 3, 5, ...)\n    # up to max_bit_pos\n    for i in range(1, max_bit_pos + 1, 2):\n        even_bits_mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Apply the mask using a bitwise OR operation\n    return num | even_bits_mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "from collections import Counter\nfrom typing import Any, List, Tuple, Dict\ndef check_occurences(input_tuples: List[Tuple[Any, Any]]) -> Dict[Tuple[Any, Any], int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts frequencies of 2-element tuples after converting them to a canonical form.\n    The canonical form of (a, b) is (min(a, b), max(a, b)).\n    \"\"\"\n    canonical_forms = []\n    for a, b in input_tuples:\n        canonical_forms.append(tuple(sorted((a, b))))\n    \n    return dict(Counter(canonical_forms))"}
