{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of possible sequences of length n,\n    where each element x_i satisfies 2 * x_{i-1} <= x_i <= m.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_length: int, last_element: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively counts valid sequences given the current state.\n        It uses memoization to store and reuse results for subproblems.\n        \"\"\"\n        if current_length == n:\n            return 1\n\n        state = (current_length, last_element)\n        if state in memo:\n            return memo[state]\n\n        count = 0\n        start_next_element = 2 * last_element\n        for next_element in range(start_next_element, m + 1):\n            count += _count_sequences_recursive(current_length + 1, next_element)\n\n        memo[state] = count\n        return count\n\n    total_sequences = 0\n    # The first element can be any positive integer from 1 to m.\n    for first_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_sequences += _count_sequences_recursive(1, first_element)\n\n    return total_sequences"}
