{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "from typing import Tuple, Union\ndef division_elements(tuple1: Tuple[Union[int, float]], tuple2: Tuple[Union[int, float]]) -> Tuple[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise integer division of two tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The numerator tuple containing int or float elements.\n        tuple2: The denominator tuple containing int or float elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple containing the integer results of the division.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If inputs are not tuples or contain non-numeric elements.\n        ValueError: If tuples have different lengths.\n        ZeroDivisionError: If any element in the second tuple is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        num1 = tuple1[i]\n        num2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(num1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(num2, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in tuples must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n        if num2 == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Cannot divide by zero.\")\n\n        # Perform integer division to match the assertion's expected output (2, 2, 2, 3).\n        results.append(num1 // num2)\n    return tuple(results)"}
