{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits the input_list into 'n' sublists, distributing elements by index modulo n.\n    Each element input_list[i] is placed into the sublist at index i % n.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The list to be split.\n        n: The integer determining the number of sublists and the splitting pattern.\n           Must be a positive integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of lists, where each inner list is one of the 'n' split lists.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If 'n' is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n    \n    result_lists: list[list] = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for i, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        result_lists[i % n].append(item)\n            \n    return result_lists"}
