{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the number is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    This function assumes valid integer input.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(abs(number))\n    \n    digit_counts = {}\n    for char_digit in num_str:\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        digit_counts[digit] = digit_counts.get(digit, 0) + 1\n        \n    for digit_val, count in digit_counts.items():\n        if count > digit_val:\n            return False\n            \n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Returns True if the condition holds for all digits, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    number_str = str(abs(number))\n    digit_counts = {}\n\n    for digit_char in number_str:\n        digit_counts[digit_char] = digit_counts.get(digit_char, 0) + 1\n\n    for digit_char, frequency in digit_counts.items():\n        digit_value = int(digit_char)\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False\n    return True"}
