{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def _kadane_algorithm(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Applies Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum contiguous subarray sum.\n    Assumes the input list 'nums' is not empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = nums[0]\n    current_max = nums[0]\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        current_max = max(nums[i], current_max + nums[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n    return max_so_far\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in the modified array\n    formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    Assumes 'arr' is not empty and 'k' is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k == 1:\n        return _kadane_algorithm(arr)\n    else:\n        total_sum_arr = sum(arr)\n        double_arr = arr + arr\n        max_sum_double = _kadane_algorithm(double_arr)\n\n        if total_sum_arr > 0:\n            return max_sum_double + (k - 2) * total_sum_arr\n        else:\n            return max_sum_double"}
