{"task_id": "Mbpp/293", "solution": "import math\ndef otherside_rightangle(a: float, b: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle given the lengths of its two legs.\n\n    Args:\n        a: The length of the first leg. Must be a positive number.\n        b: The length of the second leg. Must be a positive number.\n\n    Returns:\n        The calculated length of the hypotenuse.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If inputs are not numbers or are not positive.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input 'a'\n    if not isinstance(a, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"leg1 must be a number.\")\n    if a <= 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"leg1 must be a positive number.\")\n\n    # Validate input 'b'\n    if not isinstance(b, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"leg2 must be a number.\")\n    if b <= 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"leg2 must be a positive number.\")\n\n    hypotenuse_squared = a**2 + b**2\n    return math.sqrt(hypotenuse_squared)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/293", "solution": "import math\ndef otherside_rightangle(leg1: float, leg2: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle given the lengths of its two legs.\n    It applies the Pythagorean theorem (a\u00b2 + b\u00b2 = c\u00b2).\n    Raises TypeError if input arguments are not numerical.\n    Raises ValueError if input leg lengths are negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(leg1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(leg2, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both leg lengths must be numerical values.\")\n    if leg1 < 0 or leg2 < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Leg lengths cannot be negative.\")\n        \n    hypotenuse_squared = math.pow(leg1, 2) + math.pow(leg2, 2)\n    return float(math.sqrt(hypotenuse_squared))"}
