{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(arr):\n    # This function counts inversions using a modified merge sort algorithm.\n    # An inversion is a pair (i, j) where i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\n\n    def _merge_sort_and_count_helper(sub_arr):\n        n = len(sub_arr)\n        if n <= 1:\n            return sub_arr, 0\n\n        mid = n // 2\n        left_half, inversions_left = _merge_sort_and_count_helper(sub_arr[:mid])\n        right_half, inversions_right = _merge_sort_and_count_helper(sub_arr[mid:])\n\n        merged_array, cross_inversions = _merge_and_count_helper(left_half, right_half)\n\n        return merged_array, inversions_left + inversions_right + cross_inversions\n\n    def _merge_and_count_helper(left, right):\n        merged = []\n        inversions = 0\n        i, j = 0, 0\n        len_left = len(left)\n        len_right = len(right)\n\n        while i < len_left and j < len_right:\n            if left[i] <= right[j]:\n                merged.append(left[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                merged.append(right[j])\n                # All remaining elements in the left sub-array are greater than right[j].\n                inversions += (len_left - i)\n                j += 1\n\n        merged.extend(left[i:])\n        merged.extend(right[j:])\n\n        return merged, inversions\n\n    _, total_inversions = _merge_sort_and_count_helper(arr)\n    return total_inversions"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in an array where i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    inv_count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                inv_count += 1\n    return inv_count"}
