{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Nth Lucas number using an iterative approach.\n    It follows the definition L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2) for n > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1  # Represents L(k-2) and L(k-1) respectively, initialized to L(0) and L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n-th Lucas number based on its definition.\n    This implementation uses an iterative approach for optimal performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize with L_0 and L_1\n    a, b = 2, 1\n    # Iterate from L_2 up to L_n\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next Lucas number\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
