{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def calculate_single_number_sum(number: int) -> int:\n    # Computes the sum of the absolute digits of a single integer.\n    # Treats negative numbers as their positive counterparts.\n    s = str(abs(number))\n    digit_sum = 0\n    for digit_char in s:\n        digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n    return digit_sum\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    # Computes the total sum of digits for all numbers in a given list.\n    # It aggregates individual digit sums calculated by a helper function.\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        total_sum += calculate_single_number_sum(num)\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total sum of digits for all numbers in the provided list.\n    Trusts that the input list contains integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    overall_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        current_num_sum = 0\n        for digit_char in str(num):\n            if digit_char == '-':\n                continue\n            current_num_sum += int(digit_char)\n        overall_sum += current_num_sum\n    return overall_sum"}
