{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of integers using the Shell Sort algorithm in ascending order.\n    Returns a new sorted list, leaving the original unchanged.\"\"\"\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Create a copy to ensure the original array is not modified.\n    sorted_arr = arr[:]\n\n    # Start with a large gap and reduce it.\n    gap = n // 2\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = sorted_arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Perform insertion sort for elements at the current gap.\n            while j >= gap and sorted_arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                sorted_arr[j] = sorted_arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            sorted_arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return sorted_arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sorts the input list 'arr' in ascending order using Shell Sort.\n    Modifies the list in-place.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n // 2\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift earlier gap-sorted elements up until the correct\n            # location for arr[i] is found.\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2"}
