{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "def sumofFactors(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all even factors for a given positive integer.\n    It iterates from 1 up to the number, checking for factors that are also even.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_even_factors = 0\n    for i in range(1, number + 1):\n        if number % i == 0 and i % 2 == 0:\n            total_even_factors += i\n    return total_even_factors"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "def sumofFactors(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all even factors for a given positive integer.\n    It iterates up to the square root of the number to find factors efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_factors_sum = 0\n    # Iterate up to the integer part of the square root of the number\n    # Using number**0.5 directly to avoid calling math.sqrt which would be an external utility.\n    limit = int(number**0.5) \n    for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            # Check the first factor\n            if i % 2 == 0:\n                even_factors_sum += i\n            \n            # Check the second factor (number // i)\n            # Ensure not to double count if i * i == number (for perfect squares)\n            other_factor = number // i\n            if other_factor != i and other_factor % 2 == 0:\n                even_factors_sum += other_factor\n                \n    return even_factors_sum"}
