{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "from typing import Any, List, Optional\ndef Find_Min(list_of_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Optional[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist having the minimum length from a list of lists.\n    Returns None if the input list_of_lists is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return None\n\n    shortest_sublist = None\n    min_length = float('inf')\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            shortest_sublist = sublist\n    \n    return shortest_sublist"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a list of lists.\n    Returns the first shortest sublist encountered, or an empty list if input is empty.\"\"\"\n\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_sublist = []\n\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        \n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_sublist = sublist\n        \n    return min_sublist"}
