{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns a list of Ludic numbers less than or equal to n.\n    The sieve process iteratively removes elements based on the current Ludic number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    if n == 1:\n        return [1]\n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic_numbers = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        current_ludic = numbers.pop(0)\n        ludic_numbers.append(current_ludic)\n\n        if current_ludic == 1:\n            continue\n        \n        next_numbers = []\n        count = 0\n        for num in numbers:\n            count += 1\n            if count % current_ludic != 0:\n                next_numbers.append(num)\n        numbers = next_numbers\n            \n    return ludic_numbers"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates Ludic numbers up to a specified integer n using a sieve process.\n    The Ludic numbers are derived by sequentially removing elements from a list.\n    \"\"\"\n    ludic_numbers = []\n    candidates = list(range(1, n + 1))\n\n    while candidates:\n        l_num = candidates[0]\n        ludic_numbers.append(l_num)\n\n        elements_to_keep = []\n        # If l_num is 1, it only removes itself and doesn't strike any others.\n        # Otherwise, strike elements from the remaining candidates based on l_num.\n        if l_num == 1:\n            candidates = candidates[1:]\n        else:\n            strike_count = 0\n            for x in candidates:\n                if x == l_num:  # The current ludic number is already processed.\n                    continue\n                strike_count += 1\n                if strike_count % l_num != 0:\n                    elements_to_keep.append(x)\n            candidates = elements_to_keep\n\n    return ludic_numbers"}
