{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "_bell_cache = [[1]]\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming and memoization.\n    It builds a triangle of Stirling numbers of the second kind to compute B(n).\n\n    Args:\n        n: The non-negative integer for which to find the Bell number.\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth Bell number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Populate the Bell triangle (Stirling numbers of the second kind) up to n.\n    # The cache stores S(i,j) where i is row index and j is column index.\n    while len(_bell_cache) <= n:\n        i = len(_bell_cache)\n        new_row = [0] * (i + 1)\n        \n        # S(i, 0) = 0 for i > 0, which is handled by new_row[0] = 0.\n        # S(i, i) = 1.\n        if i == 0:\n            new_row[0] = 1 # This case is covered by the initial _bell_cache = [[1]]\n                           # but for completeness in the loop logic, it can be here.\n                           # However, 'i' in this loop starts from 1 if _bell_cache has only [1].\n            pass \n        else:\n            new_row[i] = 1 # S(i, i) = 1\n            prev_row = _bell_cache[i-1]\n            # S(i,j) = S(i-1, j-1) + j * S(i-1, j)\n            for j in range(1, i): # Loop for 1 <= j < i\n                new_row[j] = prev_row[j-1] + j * prev_row[j]\n        \n        _bell_cache.append(new_row)\n\n    # The Bell number B(n) is the sum of S(n,k) for k=0 to n.\n    return sum(_bell_cache[n])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming.\n    Memoization is used to store previously computed values for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not hasattr(bell_Number, '_memo'):\n        bell_Number._memo = {0: 1, 1: 1}\n\n    if n in bell_Number._memo:\n        return bell_Number._memo[n]\n\n    bell_triangle = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    bell_triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        bell_triangle[i][0] = bell_triangle[i - 1][i - 1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            bell_triangle[i][j] = bell_triangle[i - 1][j - 1] + bell_triangle[i][j - 1]\n    \n    result = bell_triangle[n][0]\n    bell_Number._memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
