{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coord: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the input coordinate and its 8 adjacent neighbors (including diagonals).\n    Returns a list of lists, where each inner list represents an adjacent coordinate [x, y].\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coord\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            adjacent_coords.append([x + dx, y + dy])\n    return adjacent_coords"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all 9 coordinates (the input coordinate and its 8 direct neighbors) for a given (x, y) tuple.\n    Returns a list of lists, where each inner list [x', y'] represents an adjacent coordinate.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate\n    adjacent = []\n    for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            adjacent.append([x + dx, y + dy])\n    return adjacent"}
