{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: List[Any], k: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the elements of the input list `arr` from index 0 up to `k` elements.\n    The modification is done in-place, and the modified list is returned.\"\"\"\n    if k <= 0:\n        return arr\n\n    # Determine the actual end index for reversal (exclusive).\n    # This handles k > len(arr) by reversing the entire array.\n    end_index = min(k, len(arr))\n\n    # Perform in-place reversal of the prefix using a two-pointer approach.\n    left = 0\n    right = end_index - 1\n    while left < right:\n        arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "def reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the first 'k' elements of the input list.\n    Returns a new list with the modified segment, leaving the original array unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_arr = list(arr) # Create a copy of the input list.\n    \n    # Reverse the first k elements using slice assignment with a reversed slice.\n    result_arr[0:k] = result_arr[0:k][::-1]\n\n    return result_arr"}
