{"task_id": "Mbpp/728", "solution": "def sum_list(a: list[int | float], b: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the element-wise sum of two input lists of numbers.\n\n    Args:\n        a: The first list of numbers (integers or floats).\n        b: The second list of numbers (integers or floats).\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list containing the sums of corresponding elements.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input lists are not of the same length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Lists must be of the same length\")\n\n    result_list: list[int | float] = []\n    for i in range(len(a)):\n        result_list.append(a[i] + b[i])\n    return result_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/730", "solution": "def consecutive_duplicates(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes consecutive duplicate elements from a list, returning a new list.\n    This implementation directly applies the core logic for deduplication.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    result = [input_list[0]]\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        if input_list[i] != result[-1]:\n            result.append(input_list[i])\n    return result"}
