{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "import math\ndef find_Index(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n    It calculates the lower bound and uses a quadratic formula to estimate the index.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    min_val = 10**(n - 1)\n    \n    # Calculate k_approx for k^2 + k - 2 * min_val >= 0\n    k_approx = (-1 + math.sqrt(1 + 8 * min_val)) / 2\n    \n    # Initialize k by taking the ceiling of the approximation\n    k = math.ceil(k_approx)\n    \n    # Adjust k if the calculated triangular number is too small\n    while (k * (k + 1) // 2) < min_val:\n        k += 1\n        \n    return int(k)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with `n` digits.\n    Assumes `n` is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_bound = 10**(n - 1)\n    upper_bound_exclusive = 10**n\n\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        \n        if triangular_number >= lower_bound:\n            if triangular_number < upper_bound_exclusive:\n                return k\n        k += 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "def tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple to a dictionary using adjacent elements as key-value pairs.\n    If the tuple has an odd number of elements, the last element is ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_dict = {}\n    for i in range(0, len(input_tuple) - 1, 2):\n        key = input_tuple[i]\n        value = input_tuple[i+1]\n        result_dict[key] = value\n    return result_dict"}
