{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(data_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by n positions, returning a new list.\n    Handles n values greater than list length or negative using modulo.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(data_list)\n    effective_n = n % list_length\n    \n    rotated_list = data_list[list_length - effective_n:] + data_list[:list_length - effective_n]\n    return rotated_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by n positions. Returns a new list, leaving the original unchanged.\"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    effective_n = n % list_length\n\n    if effective_n == 0:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    return input_list[-effective_n:] + input_list[:-effective_n]"}
