{"task_id": "Mbpp/749", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef sort_numeric_strings(numeric_strings: List[str]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of strings representing numbers numerically in ascending order.\n    This function trusts that all input elements are valid integer representations.\n    \"\"\"\n    converted_numbers = []\n    for s in numeric_strings:\n        # Converts each string element to an integer.\n        # Per critical requirements, no explicit type checks or custom exception handling is performed here.\n        converted_numbers.append(int(s))\n    \n    # Sorts the list of integers numerically.\n    converted_numbers.sort()\n    \n    return converted_numbers"}
