{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "def extract_index_list(l1: list, l2: list, l3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies elements common to three lists at the same index.\n    Iteration is limited by the length of the shortest input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    common_elements = []\n    min_length = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n\n    for i in range(min_length):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            common_elements.append(l1[i])\n\n    return common_elements"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "def extract_index_list(l1: list, l2: list, l3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements that are common to all three lists at the same index.\n    It iterates up to the length of the shortest list to prevent IndexError.\n    \"\"\"\n    common_elements = []\n    min_length = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n\n    for i in range(min_length):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            common_elements.append(l1[i])\n    return common_elements"}
