{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "def find_min_diff(arr: tuple, n: int) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the input tuple.\n    Returns 0 if the tuple has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Convert to list for sorting and find the minimum difference between adjacent elements.\n    sorted_arr = sorted(list(arr))\n    \n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        diff = sorted_arr[i] - sorted_arr[i-1]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n    \n    return min_diff"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "def find_min_diff(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum difference between any two elements in a given array.\n    The array is assumed to contain numeric elements and n is its correct length >= 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a sorted copy of the array for efficient difference calculation.\n    sorted_arr = sorted(arr)\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through adjacent elements to find the smallest difference.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        diff = sorted_arr[i+1] - sorted_arr[i]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n    \n    return min_diff"}
