{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position (highest index) of an element in a sorted array.\n    Returns the highest index if found, otherwise -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return -1\n\n    low, high = 0, len(array) - 1\n    last_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            last_index = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return last_index"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list[int], element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the last index of the element if found, otherwise -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
