{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a left bitwise rotation on a 32-bit unsigned integer.\n    The number is treated as 32 bits, and the rotation amount d is taken modulo 32.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_LENGTH = 32\n    MAX_VALUE = 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    d_effective = d % BIT_LENGTH\n    num_32bit = number & MAX_VALUE\n\n    rotated = (num_32bit << d_effective) | (num_32bit >> (BIT_LENGTH - d_effective))\n    return rotated & MAX_VALUE"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "BITS_IN_INT = 32\nMAX_32BIT_VALUE = 0xFFFFFFFF\ndef left_rotate(n: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit integer 'n' to the left by 'd' positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure d is within the valid range [0, BITS_IN_INT - 1] for rotation.\n    d = d % BITS_IN_INT\n\n    # Perform left rotation using shifts and a final mask for 32 bits.\n    return ((n << d) | (n >> (BITS_IN_INT - d))) & MAX_32BIT_VALUE"}
